Origin of the files in this folder (reference copy: /workspace/vo-ref/src/VanphongAI-main/app/public, read-only).
The reference is written with Vietnamese identifiers, CSS class names and UI strings. Our port translates all of them to English
(e.g. dungNguoi → buildPerson, khoi → block, vatLieu → material, chuanHoa → normalizeLook, MAU_SAN → PRESETS, datNgayDem → setNight,
gocMacDinh → defaultView, .nguoi-3d → .person-3d, .ten-3d → .name-3d, .bong-3d → .bubble-3d, --nhan → --accent, preset ids nam_01/nu_01 →
male_01/female_01); the reference names below and in code comments are kept so each piece can still be traced back.
- characters.ts  <- van_phong_3d.js (dungNguoi, toc, phuKien, khoi) + nhan_vat.js (chuanHoa, tronMau, presets).
                    Geometry, colours and hair/accessory recipes copied verbatim; converted to a typed ES module using npm `three`,
                    identifiers and preset values in English.
- scene.ts       <- van_phong_3d.js (anhSan, cayCanh, cuaSo, dungNen, choNgoi, dungPhong, capNhatNguoi, bayPhieu,
                    datNgayDem, camera/zoom helpers). Copied with adaptations: driven by our reducer state, our walker
                    (web/src/walk.ts) instead of the help-desk route map, no server room / store-room door / reception / lobby.
                    Ours: gocMacDinh's camera fit, the idle poses (coffee, billiards, chat, scuffle), freeSince tracking and the
                    pantry/game-room (amenities.ts) wiring.
- office3d.css   <- style.css (:root palette, .nguoi-3d / .ten-3d / .bong-3d / .zzz-3d / .nhan-phong-3d / .nut-3d / .vp3d-*),
                    scoped under .office3d-ref (was :root), with every custom property and class renamed to English (.person-3d, .name-3d,
                    .bubble-3d, .room-label-3d, .btn-3d, .office3d-*). Rules otherwise verbatim except dropped selectors; the .scuffle bubble rule is ours.
- avatars.ts     <- nhan_vat.js (chibi SVG avatar `ve` → drawAvatar, `chuanHoa` → normalizeLook, the 20 presets MAU_SAN → PRESETS). Drawing
                    recipes verbatim; identifiers, SVG class names and preset names translated to English, the IIFE/window global became ES exports.
                    Used for town avatars and the name/avatar picker (same flow as cai_dat.js moChonMau: Female/Male tabs, preset grid).
- adapter.ts     <- new code (ours): maps our AgentUI/MessageUI to the reference's display states; wider desk grid, pantry/game-room
                    layout and the idle behaviour (coffee, billiards, chats, scuffles) of free agents.
- amenities.ts   <- new code (ours): pantry (coffee machine, fridge, tables) and game room (billiard table, arcade, sofa), built with
                    the reference's voxel helpers (block/material, ref. khoi/vatLieu) so they match its look.
- town3d.ts      <- new code (ours): the town around the office (roads, Crossian Cafe, iced tea stall, croc pond, IT Ops kiosk,
                    side characters and pets), built with the reference's voxel helpers (block/material/buildPerson) so it matches its look.
                    The menu/editor UI (web/src/town/Editor.tsx) is ours too, following cai_dat.js moChonMau.
The reference's vendored three.js (MIT, see its LICENSE) is NOT copied; we use our npm `three` (MIT).
